{"game_id":2026020224,"away":"TOR","home":"VAN","split":{"name":"Schenn","side":1,"sec":2636},"lede":"Vancouver had last change, so Manny Malhotra picked most of these matchups. Vancouver played without Arshdeep Bains and Filip Chytil and lost Luke Schenn after 3:56 of the third. Toronto played without Kirill Marchenko and Dakota Mermis.","notes":[{"kind":"match","head":"The third line drew Joshua’s line","text":"Manny Malhotra sent Öhgren, Quillan and Karlsson out for 7:08 of their 10:25 at 5-on-5 against McKenna, Sissons and Joshua (68%, about 23% with no line matching), and they had the worse of the chances, 0.09 to 0.40 expected goals."},{"kind":"match","head":"E. Pettersson’s line drew Nylander’s line","text":"DeBrusk, E. Pettersson and Boeser spent 8:41 of their 12:01 at 5-on-5 against Nylander, Matthews and Roslovic (72%, about 32% with no line matching), and they had the worse of the chances, 0.09 to 0.26 expected goals. Toronto scored one of its four goals then."},{"kind":"match","head":"Rossi’s line drew Cowan’s line","text":"O'Connor, Rossi and Lekkerimäki spent 5:53 of their 11:38 at 5-on-5 against Cowan, Paul and Lettieri (51%, about 25% with no line matching), and they had the better of the chances, 0.88 to 0.47 expected goals."},{"kind":"exit","head":"After Schenn left, the lines changed","text":"Sasson went from 20% to 37% and Cotter from 20% to 35% of Vancouver’s 5-on-5 time, and Quillan dropped from 28% to 15%. The matchups changed: E. Pettersson’s line against Toronto’s first line (84% before, 18% after) and Rossi’s line against Toronto’s second line (55% before, 34% after)."},{"kind":"result","head":"And it went better","text":"Vancouver had 1.22 to 2.10 expected goals at 5-on-5 before Schenn left and 0.40 to 0.14 after. Vancouver trailed for most of that stretch, though, and a team behind usually pushes the play, so the score explains part of it."}],"foot":"Manny Malhotra matched about as hard as in his other home games: each line spent 57% of i